":713},{"seed":5082,"score":924.3999999999817,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":756},{"seed":5083,"score":935.9999999999909,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":640},{"seed":5084,"score":932.6999999999887,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":673},{"seed":5085,"score":922.2999999999898,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":777},{"seed":5086,"score":935.7999999999876,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":642},{"seed":5087,"score":158.92857142857684,"tiles":0.25892857142857145,"lap":false,"steps":1000},{"seed":5088,"score":872.2222222221992,"tiles":0.9722222222222222,"lap":false,"steps":1000},{"seed":5089,"score":931.9999999999844,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":680},{"seed":5090,"score":939.6999999999946,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":603},{"seed":5091,"score":922.2999999999832,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":777},{"seed":5092,"score":937.6999999999867,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":623},{"seed":5093,"score":938.4999999999887,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":615},{"seed":5094,"score":937.0999999999851,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":629},{"seed":5095,"score":565.5290102388877,"tiles":0.6655290102389079,"lap":false,"steps":1000},{"seed":5096,"score":927.7999999999824,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":722},{"seed":5097,"score":927.5999999999874,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":724},{"seed":5098,"score":934.7999999999854,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":652},{"seed":5099,"score":924.4999999999835,"tiles":1.0,"lap":true,"steps":755}],"replay":"replays/goal_goal_r1_1.1M.gif"},{"t":"2026-11-10 21:13:51","title":"Picked up again: the v1 agent was blind","text":"Reading the v1 code (Dec 2025) found three silent bugs. (1) The lidar read 0 on every ray: it looked for polygons in env.road, which holds Box2D bodies, so no point was ever 'on the road'. (2) 'Traction' was always 1: wheels have no ground_contact attribute (they keep a set of touched tiles), so the off-track penalty never fired. (3) The +500 finish bonus waited for info['finished_track'], a key CarRacing never sets (it says lap_finished). The agent saw only its speed and compass heading. Scored with CarRacing's own reward on 100 unseen tracks, the v1 best model averages -42.9 (best -7.6) and covers 6.5% of a track.","kind":"journal"},{"t":"2026-11-10 21:13:51","title":"Speed: 99% of a step was drawing a picture nobody looked at","text":"CarRacing draws its 96x96 state image inside every step(): 8.0 ms of a 9.4 ms step. Box2D's physics alone is 0.09 ms. Training now skips that drawing (videos still render), and a test checks the world stays bit-identical. The new lidar was chosen by a bake-off of six implementations (pure Python, NumPy, numba, C++, Rust, Go): all bit-identical on 900 poses x 19 rays; numba won (no build step, same source as the reference). A full env step is now ~0.5 ms.","kind":"journal"},{"t":"2026-11-10 21:13:51","title":"v2: new eyes, PPO, the real score","text":"New 49-number observation: speed, sideways slip, yaw rate, steer, which wheels are on the road, offset and heading against the centre line, 8 centre-line points up to 40 tiles ahead, and 19 lidar rays that work. Two-axis action (steer; gas or brake). Training reward = CarRacing's own score, so training aims at the metric; stage 1 stops hopeless episodes early (-50). PPO with observation and reward normalisation, time-limit bootstrapping. First run: validation 457 at 0.1 M steps.","kind":"journal"}]